   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Purpose",
     "texto": [
      "**-기 위해서** expresses the purpose of an action: 공부하다 → **공부하기 위해서** (in order to study), 합격하다 → **합격하기 위해서** (in order to pass), 돈을 벌다 → **돈을 벌기 위해서** (in order to earn money).",
      "시험에 **합격하기 위해서** 공부해요 = I study in order to pass the exam."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Difference with -(으)러",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)러** (A2) expresses the purpose of a movement and usually goes with verbs like 가다/오다: 도서관에 공부하러 가요 = I go to the library to study. **-기 위해서** is used to indicate the goal of various actions. It is not an opposition of informal versus formal; the level of politeness is marked by the sentence ending."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
